chosen:
Claim status: GC-512407 is in the Inspection stage, and your PhotoEstimate photos have been received.
Next step: Your estimate will post in ClaimTrack within 2 business days of the upload, and Granite Mobile will notify you when it does.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will call you to review the estimate once it posts. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: SafeMiles gives a 5% discount as soon as you enroll. After the 90-day scoring period, your renewal discount follows your SafeMiles score: 90+ earns 25%, 80–89 earns 15%, 70–79 earns 10%, and below 70 you keep the 5%. It never raises your premium.
Next step: Enroll in Granite Mobile > SafeMiles; the SafeMiles Tag SM-200 ships within 5 business days.
Who will contact you: The SafeMiles team will message you with tracking once your tag ships. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Payments made within 10 days of the due date are inside the grace period and shouldn't carry the $10 late fee, so this looks like an error.
Next step: I've opened a billing dispute for the fee; disputes are reviewed within 1 business day, and the refund posts in 3–5 business days.
Who will contact you: Felix Arundel's Policy Service & Billing team will confirm the reversal in Granite Mobile within 1 business day. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: It depends on your auto tier: Granite Auto Plus covers $40/day and Premier covers $60/day, each for up to 30 days. Basic doesn't include rental unless you added the $4/month rental endorsement ($30/day).
Next step: Check your tier on the declarations page in Granite Mobile > Policy > Documents, and keep any rental receipts for ClaimTrack.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will confirm rental authorization within 24 hours of your claim report. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Your claim is Paid. HomeShield dwelling payments over $10,000 must list the mortgage company as co-payee, so we can't remove them from this check.
Next step: Send the check to your mortgage company's loss draft department for endorsement; many release funds in stages as repairs are completed.
Who will contact you: Your property adjuster can send the lender a copy of the estimate; message them in ClaimTrack and they'll reply within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Yes, in most cases. When the other driver is at fault, we pursue subrogation against their insurer.
Next step: Nothing is needed from you once the claim is filed. Your deductible is refunded in proportion to what we recover, typically within 60–120 days.
Who will contact you: The auto claims team will message you in Granite Mobile when the recovery posts. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: HomeShield Essential pays contents at actual cash value, covers additional living expenses for up to 6 months, and doesn't include water backup. HomeShield Plus pays contents at replacement cost, covers additional living expenses for up to 12 months, and includes $10,000 of water backup coverage.
Next step: Compare both in Granite Mobile under Policy > Coverages.
Who will contact you: Reply 'quote' and Policy Service will send you a Plus quote within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Roadside assistance is included on Granite Auto Plus (towing up to 15 miles) and Premier (up to 50 miles); Basic doesn't include it.
Next step: If you're on Plus or Premier, request help in Granite Mobile > Roadside or call the 24/7 Claims Line at 555-0186.
Who will contact you: The roadside provider will text you an arrival time as soon as the request is dispatched. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Once you sign the settlement in ClaimTrack, payment is issued within 5 business days.
Next step: Choose direct deposit in ClaimTrack for funds 1–2 business days after issue; a mailed check takes 7–10 business days.
Who will contact you: Your adjuster will reply in ClaimTrack within 4 business hours if you have questions about the amount. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Yes, glass is covered. A small chip repair is $0 deductible on every tier; a full windshield replacement on Granite Auto Plus uses your comprehensive deductible (only Premier has $0 replacement).
Next step: Report it in Granite Mobile under Claims > Report a Claim > Glass with a photo, and we'll confirm whether it can be repaired or needs replacement.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will follow up within 24 hours of the report. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Your HomeShield claim is Assigned. The hailstorm was declared a CAT event, so adjuster visits are scheduled within 5 business days instead of the usual 3.
Next step: If there's an active leak, call the Claims Line at 555-0186 for Granite Rapid Response tarping; emergency mitigation is reimbursed up to $2,500 without pre-approval. Upload damage photos to ClaimTrack meanwhile.
Who will contact you: Your property adjuster will confirm the visit time by phone within 72 hours of your report. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: You can mark a trip "I wasn't driving" within 7 days of the trip.
Next step: In Granite Mobile, go to SafeMiles > Trips, select the trip and tap "I wasn't driving"; your SafeMiles score recalculates without it.
Who will contact you: No call needed. If a trip is past 7 days or the option is missing, reply here and the SafeMiles team will respond within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Yes. HomeShield all-perils deductible options are $500, $1,000 and $2,500. The change takes effect the next day and doesn't apply to any open claims.
Next step: Choose $2,500 in Granite Mobile under Policy > Coverages; you'll see the premium savings before you confirm.
Who will contact you: Policy Service will confirm and post your updated declarations page within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Additional damage found during repairs is handled as a supplement to your existing estimate.
Next step: Ask the shop to submit the supplement with photos through ClaimTrack. Supplements are reviewed within 2 business days.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will contact you and the shop with the decision within 2 business days of receiving it. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Yes. There's no cancellation fee, and any unused premium is refunded pro rata within 10 business days of the cancellation date.
Next step: Make sure your new coverage starts before this policy ends, then call Customer Care at 555-0129 to set the date.
Who will contact you: Policy Service will send your cancellation confirmation to Granite Mobile, and the refund follows within 10 business days. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: No. You have a 10-day grace period after the due date, so paying 9 days late keeps your coverage active with no $10 late fee.
Next step: Pay in Granite Mobile > Billing by the end of the grace period. Setting up autopay also waives the $5 installment fee going forward.
Who will contact you: No call needed; you'll get a payment confirmation in Granite Mobile as soon as it's made. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Your claim stays in your name, but you can authorize him to discuss it.
Next step: Add him in ClaimTrack under Claim > Contacts with his name, phone and email. Once he's listed, the adjuster can talk with him directly.
Who will contact you: Your adjuster will reply in ClaimTrack within 4 business hours to confirm. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Not reported yet. Pothole damage is handled under collision coverage, with your collision deductible.
Next step: Report it in Granite Mobile, then use PhotoEstimate (8 photos) or drive in to a Drive-In Claim Center in Cedar Bluff, Ridgeview or Lowell Flats (Mon–Fri 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. MT). If the car isn't safe to drive, request a tow in Granite Mobile > Roadside if you're on Plus or Premier.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will call within 24 hours of the report. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Your declarations page is always available in Granite Mobile under Policy > Documents, where you can download or share it as a PDF.
Next step: If you need it sent to a lender, reply with the lender's name and mortgagee clause; we send evidence of insurance to lenders directly within 2 business days.
Who will contact you: Policy Service will reply here within 4 business hours if you need anything else. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Your SafeMiles score and discount are safe while we sort this out.
Next step: Request a replacement in Granite Mobile > SafeMiles > Device > Replace Tag. The SafeMiles Tag SM-200 replacement is free once per policy term ($15 after that) and ships within 5 business days.
Who will contact you: The SafeMiles team will message you with tracking once it ships. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: For HomeShield claims, your adjuster makes first contact within 48 hours of the report (72 hours during a declared CAT event).
Next step: The adjuster visit is scheduled within 3 business days (5 during a CAT event). Upload photos to ClaimTrack in the meantime.
Who will contact you: Your assigned property adjuster, by phone, within those 48 hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: The water backup endorsement for HomeShield Essential costs $6/month and covers up to $5,000 of sewer or drain backup damage.
Next step: Add it in Granite Mobile under Policy > Coverages; you'll see the price change before confirming.
Who will contact you: Policy Service will confirm and post your updated declarations page within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: No. Drive-In Claim Centers in Cedar Bluff, Ridgeview and Lowell Flats are open Mon–Fri 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. MT, no appointment needed.
Next step: If weekdays don't work, use PhotoEstimate in Granite Mobile any time (8 photos), and your estimate posts within 2 business days.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will call you once your estimate is posted. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Since the car can't be driven, an adjuster will come to inspect it where it is; PhotoEstimate and the drive-in centers aren't needed.
Next step: Make sure the claim is reported in Granite Mobile and confirm the address in ClaimTrack.
Who will contact you: Your auto adjuster will call within 24 hours of the report, and the inspection will happen within 3 business days. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: Monthly installments carry a $5 installment fee, which is waived if you use autopay (EFT). You would no longer receive the 6% pay-in-full discount.
Next step: Change your plan in Granite Mobile under Billing > Payment Plan and turn on autopay to avoid the fee.
Who will contact you: Billing will confirm your new schedule in Granite Mobile within 4 business hours. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Not reported yet. Damage to your fence is claimed on your own HomeShield policy. Because it was wind damage, your wind/hail deductible (2% of Coverage A) applies; if the tree was clearly neglected, your adjuster will review whether we can recover from the neighbor's insurer.
Next step: Report the claim in Granite Mobile and upload photos of the tree and the fence to ClaimTrack.
Who will contact you: A property adjuster will call within 48 hours of the report. {{SIGNOFF}}

Policy status: SafeMiles never raises your premium. Your renewal discount follows your score: 90+ earns 25%, 80–89 earns 15%, 70–79 earns 10%, and below 70 you keep the 5% enrollment discount.
Next step: Check your score and recent trips in Granite Mobile > SafeMiles, and flag any trip you didn't drive within 7 days.
Who will contact you: The SafeMiles team will reply here within 4 business hours if you have questions about a trip. {{SIGNOFF}}

Claim status: Your claim is in the Settlement stage. Because this is a dwelling payment over $10,000, your mortgage company must be listed as co-payee, so it will be issued as a check rather than direct deposit.
Next step: Sign the settlement in ClaimTrack; payment is issued within 5 business days and the mailed check takes 7–10 business days. Contents and ALE payments can still go to you by direct deposit.
Who will contact you: Your property adjuster will reply in ClaimTrack within 4 business hours with your lender's loss draft details. {{SIGNOFF}}
